    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "s1_title",
      "x": 120, "y": 40,
      "width": 1400, "height": 50,
      "text": "How the pipeline guesses WHERE a photo was taken (and why it is built this way)",
      "originalText": "How the pipeline guesses WHERE a photo was taken (and why it is built this way)",
      "fontSize": 34, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1e40af", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 100001,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 100002, "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false,
      "containerId": null, "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "s1_subtitle",
      "x": 120, "y": 100,
      "width": 1400, "height": 60,
      "text": "The computer never 'knows' the location. It keeps a table of guesses with confidence numbers, looks at the photo for clues,\nand nudges those numbers up or down. It repeats this from a rough guess (which continent?) down to a precise one (which street?).",
      "originalText": "The computer never 'knows' the location. It keeps a table of guesses with confidence numbers, looks at the photo for clues,\nand nudges those numbers up or down. It repeats this from a rough guess (which continent?) down to a precise one (which street?).",
      "fontSize": 18, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#64748b", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 100003,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 100004, "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false,
      "containerId": null, "lineHeight": 1.35
    },

