    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "id": "s3_formula",
      "x": 730, "y": 1470, "width": 690, "height": 165,
      "strokeColor": "#6d28d9", "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 300021,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 300022, "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [], "boundElements": [{"id": "s3_formula_t", "type": "text"}],
      "link": null, "locked": false, "roundness": {"type": 3}
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "s3_formula_t",
      "x": 748, "y": 1486, "width": 655, "height": 135,
      "text": "THE ACTUAL FORMULA  (modules/sl.py, _reduce)\n\n  W_sl = exp[ a_mean * beta * (c_mean - 3) * (1 - lambda * sigma_c) ]\n\n     c_mean  = average score over the 5 samples\n     sigma_c = spread (std-dev) of the 5 samples\n     lambda  = uncertainty penalty (default 1.0)\n\n  Low spread  -> (1 - lambda*sigma) near 1  -> full-strength score\n  High spread -> factor shrinks toward 0      -> score pulled to neutral\n  (floored at 0.3 so it never fully vanishes)",
      "originalText": "THE ACTUAL FORMULA  (modules/sl.py, _reduce)\n\n  W_sl = exp[ a_mean * beta * (c_mean - 3) * (1 - lambda * sigma_c) ]\n\n     c_mean  = average score over the 5 samples\n     sigma_c = spread (std-dev) of the 5 samples\n     lambda  = uncertainty penalty (default 1.0)\n\n  Low spread  -> (1 - lambda*sigma) near 1  -> full-strength score\n  High spread -> factor shrinks toward 0      -> score pulled to neutral\n  (floored at 0.3 so it never fully vanishes)",
      "fontSize": 13, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#22c55e", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 300023,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 300024, "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false,
      "containerId": "s3_formula", "lineHeight": 1.4
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "id": "s3_failure",
      "x": 120, "y": 1680, "width": 640, "height": 150,
      "strokeColor": "#b91c1c", "backgroundColor": "#fecaca",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 300025,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 300026, "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [], "boundElements": [{"id": "s3_failure_t", "type": "text"}],
      "link": null, "locked": false, "roundness": {"type": 3}
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "s3_failure_t",
      "x": 138, "y": 1696, "width": 604, "height": 120,
      "text": "!! THE CATCH (why SL alone is not enough)\n\nSL assumes 'unsure = the samples disagree'. But the 7B model is often\nCONFIDENTLY WRONG: it says '5,5,5,5,5' for the WRONG country. The\nspread is tiny, so SL sees 'confident' and does NOT shrink -- it lets a\nwrong-but-consistent answer through at full strength. Agreement is not\nthe same as correctness. This is why the coarse levels still make US-bias\nmistakes, and motivates the fixes in the last section.",
      "originalText": "!! THE CATCH (why SL alone is not enough)\n\nSL assumes 'unsure = the samples disagree'. But the 7B model is often\nCONFIDENTLY WRONG: it says '5,5,5,5,5' for the WRONG country. The\nspread is tiny, so SL sees 'confident' and does NOT shrink -- it lets a\nwrong-but-consistent answer through at full strength. Agreement is not\nthe same as correctness. This is why the coarse levels still make US-bias\nmistakes, and motivates the fixes in the last section.",
      "fontSize": 13, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#7f1d1d", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 300027,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 300028, "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false,
      "containerId": "s3_failure", "lineHeight": 1.35
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "id": "s3_knob",
      "x": 800, "y": 1680, "width": 620, "height": 150,
      "strokeColor": "#1e40af", "backgroundColor": "#dbeafe",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 300029,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 300030, "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [], "boundElements": [{"id": "s3_knob_t", "type": "text"}],
      "link": null, "locked": false, "roundness": {"type": 3}
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "s3_knob_t",
      "x": 818, "y": 1696, "width": 584, "height": 120,
      "text": "THE FIX-KNOB:  SL_DISABLE_LEVELS\n\nBecause the shrink-when-unsure trick backfires at coarse levels, we can\nswitch SL OFF there (one sample, no shrink -> plain GeoBayes score) while\nkeeping it ON for city/street where sample-disagreement is meaningful.\n\nThe better fix (research direction): replace 'spread' with a SEMANTIC\ncheck -- do the samples MEAN the same place? -- so confident-but-wrong\ncan finally be caught. (semantic-entropy, Farquhar Nature 2024.)",
      "originalText": "THE FIX-KNOB:  SL_DISABLE_LEVELS\n\nBecause the shrink-when-unsure trick backfires at coarse levels, we can\nswitch SL OFF there (one sample, no shrink -> plain GeoBayes score) while\nkeeping it ON for city/street where sample-disagreement is meaningful.\n\nThe better fix (research direction): replace 'spread' with a SEMANTIC\ncheck -- do the samples MEAN the same place? -- so confident-but-wrong\ncan finally be caught. (semantic-entropy, Farquhar Nature 2024.)",
      "fontSize": 13, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1e3a8a", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 300031,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 300032, "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false,
      "containerId": "s3_knob", "lineHeight": 1.35
    },
