    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "id": "s4_insight",
      "x": 960, "y": 2020, "width": 460, "height": 200,
      "strokeColor": "#b45309", "backgroundColor": "#fef3c7",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 400021,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 400022, "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [], "boundElements": [{"id": "s4_insight_t", "type": "text"}],
      "link": null, "locked": false, "roundness": {"type": 3}
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "s4_insight_t",
      "x": 978, "y": 2036, "width": 424, "height": 170,
      "text": "KEY THESIS INSIGHT  (why DST is disabled at coarse levels)\n\nClassic Dempster-Shafer fusion divides by (1 - K) and re-normalizes\nafter every step. That normalization THROWS AWAY the raw magnitude\nof the evidence -- it only keeps relative shape.\n\nAt continent/country, the whole game is the STRENGTH of the\n'North America vs Europe' contrast. Normalizing flattens exactly that\ncontrast, making a strong signal look weak. So at coarse levels we\nturn the fancy fusion OFF and use plain multiply, which preserves it.",
      "originalText": "KEY THESIS INSIGHT  (why DST is disabled at coarse levels)\n\nClassic Dempster-Shafer fusion divides by (1 - K) and re-normalizes\nafter every step. That normalization THROWS AWAY the raw magnitude\nof the evidence -- it only keeps relative shape.\n\nAt continent/country, the whole game is the STRENGTH of the\n'North America vs Europe' contrast. Normalizing flattens exactly that\ncontrast, making a strong signal look weak. So at coarse levels we\nturn the fancy fusion OFF and use plain multiply, which preserves it.",
      "fontSize": 12, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#78350f", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 400023,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 400024, "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false,
      "containerId": "s4_insight", "lineHeight": 1.35
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "id": "s4_debias",
      "x": 120, "y": 2270, "width": 640, "height": 170,
      "strokeColor": "#6d28d9", "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 400025,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 400026, "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [], "boundElements": [{"id": "s4_debias_t", "type": "text"}],
      "link": null, "locked": false, "roundness": {"type": 3}
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "s4_debias_t",
      "x": 138, "y": 2286, "width": 604, "height": 140,
      "text": "BONUS JOB: fighting the USA-bias directly  (_debias_country_prior)\n\n  P'(country) = P(country) / freq(country) ^ gamma\n\nThe model over-guesses countries it saw a lot in training (USA most of\nall). We divide each country's confidence by how COMMON it is, raised\nto a dial 'gamma'. Common countries get pushed down; rare ones get a\nfair chance. gamma = 0 turns it off. (COUNTRY_PRIOR_DEBIAS_GAMMA)",
      "originalText": "BONUS JOB: fighting the USA-bias directly  (_debias_country_prior)\n\n  P'(country) = P(country) / freq(country) ^ gamma\n\nThe model over-guesses countries it saw a lot in training (USA most of\nall). We divide each country's confidence by how COMMON it is, raised\nto a dial 'gamma'. Common countries get pushed down; rare ones get a\nfair chance. gamma = 0 turns it off. (COUNTRY_PRIOR_DEBIAS_GAMMA)",
      "fontSize": 12, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#22c55e", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 400027,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 400028, "isDeleted": false,
