      "containerId": "s5_reward", "lineHeight": 1.25
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "id": "s5_formula",
      "x": 120, "y": 2830, "width": 700, "height": 300,
      "strokeColor": "#6d28d9", "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 500023,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 500024, "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [], "boundElements": [{"id": "s5_formula_t", "type": "text"}],
      "link": null, "locked": false, "roundness": {"type": 3}
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "s5_formula_t",
      "x": 138, "y": 2846, "width": 665, "height": 270,
      "text": "HOW A CLUE IS SCORED BEFORE WE PAY FOR IT  (default: eig)\n\nFor each candidate clue a, IMAGINE running it:\n  1. ask the model to PREDICT the 1-5 score for each top guess\n  2. for every possible score o, compute the table b' it WOULD produce\n  3. reward that outcome by how much cleaner b' is than b\n\n  Reward(b,a,o) =\n       lambda_H [ H(b)  - H(b') ]     <- entropy drop (less confusion)\n     + lambda_M [ maxP(b') - maxP(b) ] <- top guess got stronger\n     + lambda_G [ margin(b') - margin(b) ] <- winner pulls ahead of 2nd\n     - cost(a)\n\n  Q(b,a) = sum_o  P(o | b,a) * Reward(...)      <- average over outcomes\n\nPICK the clue with the highest Q. (config: POMDP_*_WEIGHT dials each term;\nsimpler modes 'entropy' / 'map_gain' keep just one term for ablations.)",
      "originalText": "HOW A CLUE IS SCORED BEFORE WE PAY FOR IT  (default: eig)\n\nFor each candidate clue a, IMAGINE running it:\n  1. ask the model to PREDICT the 1-5 score for each top guess\n  2. for every possible score o, compute the table b' it WOULD produce\n  3. reward that outcome by how much cleaner b' is than b\n\n  Reward(b,a,o) =\n       lambda_H [ H(b)  - H(b') ]     <- entropy drop (less confusion)\n     + lambda_M [ maxP(b') - maxP(b) ] <- top guess got stronger\n     + lambda_G [ margin(b') - margin(b) ] <- winner pulls ahead of 2nd\n     - cost(a)\n\n  Q(b,a) = sum_o  P(o | b,a) * Reward(...)      <- average over outcomes\n\nPICK the clue with the highest Q. (config: POMDP_*_WEIGHT dials each term;\nsimpler modes 'entropy' / 'map_gain' keep just one term for ablations.)",
      "fontSize": 12, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#22c55e", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 500025,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 500026, "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false,
      "containerId": "s5_formula", "lineHeight": 1.4
    },

    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "s5_entropy_note",
      "x": 860, "y": 2846, "width": 560, "height": 100,
      "text": "WHAT IS 'ENTROPY' H(b)?  Just a confusion score for the table.\n\n  Flat table [0.33, 0.33, 0.33]  -> HIGH entropy (totally unsure)\n  Peaked table [0.9, 0.05, 0.05] -> LOW entropy  (nearly decided)\n\nA good clue is one that we expect to DROP the entropy a lot -- it turns a\nflat, unsure table into a peaked, decided one. That is 'information gain'.",
      "originalText": "WHAT IS 'ENTROPY' H(b)?  Just a confusion score for the table.\n\n  Flat table [0.33, 0.33, 0.33]  -> HIGH entropy (totally unsure)\n  Peaked table [0.9, 0.05, 0.05] -> LOW entropy  (nearly decided)\n\nA good clue is one that we expect to DROP the entropy a lot -- it turns a\nflat, unsure table into a peaked, decided one. That is 'information gain'.",
      "fontSize": 13, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#64748b", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 500027,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 500028, "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false,
      "containerId": null, "lineHeight": 1.4
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "id": "s5_fixed",
      "x": 860, "y": 2970, "width": 560, "height": 160,
      "strokeColor": "#1e40af", "backgroundColor": "#dbeafe",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 500029,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 500030, "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [], "boundElements": [{"id": "s5_fixed_t", "type": "text"}],
      "link": null, "locked": false, "roundness": {"type": 3}
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "s5_fixed_t",
      "x": 878, "y": 2986, "width": 524, "height": 130,
      "text": "THE FIX-KNOB:  POMDP_COARSE_FIXED_ORDER\n\nAt continent/country the clever 'chase the biggest entropy drop' plan\nbackfired: the 7B model can't reliably resolve the clue it picks, so it\nchases noise and regressed earlier versions. So at coarse levels we\nDROP the adaptive choice and just run clues in a FIXED sensible order\n(climate -> hemisphere -> script, per GeoCoT). Adaptive POMDP stays\non for city/street, where the model's answers are trustworthy enough\nfor the smart selection to pay off. Also: 'llm' mode lets the model\nitself pick, as a lightweight fallback.",
      "originalText": "THE FIX-KNOB:  POMDP_COARSE_FIXED_ORDER\n\nAt continent/country the clever 'chase the biggest entropy drop' plan\nbackfired: the 7B model can't reliably resolve the clue it picks, so it\nchases noise and regressed earlier versions. So at coarse levels we\nDROP the adaptive choice and just run clues in a FIXED sensible order\n(climate -> hemisphere -> script, per GeoCoT). Adaptive POMDP stays\non for city/street, where the model's answers are trustworthy enough\nfor the smart selection to pay off. Also: 'llm' mode lets the model\nitself pick, as a lightweight fallback.",
      "fontSize": 12, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1e3a8a", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 500031,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 500032, "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false,
      "containerId": "s5_fixed", "lineHeight": 1.35
    },
    {
      "type": "line",
      "id": "s5_divider",
      "x": 120, "y": 3180, "width": 1450, "height": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#64748b", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0, "seed": 500033,
      "version": 1, "versionNonce": 500034, "isDeleted": false,
